  "summary": "xblaxw beacons host identifiers to hardcoded bare-IP endpoint on install and require",
  "details": "The package is a stub with no legitimate functionality. Its postinstall hook runs beacon.cjs, and index.js (the main entry) invokes beacon.fire() on require. Both paths POST hostname, install path, cwd, Node version, and package name over cleartext HTTP to the hardcoded bare-IP endpoint http://185.158.107.175:8787/_ah/dc. The module's only export is a Proxy of no-op functions, so consumers importing xblaxw receive non-functional stubs while triggering the beacon. No opt-in, no publisher-matching domain, no legitimate purpose served by the fetched endpoint.",
